From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:28:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 067/147] hjviewer: toasts, and confirms that can lock a PC out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U29: hjvConfirmDialog takes danger: the title with a warning icon in
the danger colour and the action in deleteConfirmDialog's look (the
danger fill on a desktop, the danger colour on a phone). The logout
dialog (L1) has the title "로그아웃할까요?" and [로그아웃]; on a PC this
login bound the gate's line and the binding's end are one sentence,
the remote use is a warning note below it, and the question no longer
repeats. Removing a PC (L2), a device's logout, all other devices',
turning password-less connections off and the remote restart use the
danger look; the restart's action is [다시 시작]. L2 says "그 PC"
throughout. A2's icon is red, and a recent card's [삭제] says "최근
목록에서 지우기".

U45: showToast draws hjv_style.dart's HjvToast: the theme's snack bar
colours, opaque, Pretendard 14 w500, radius 10, at most 480 wide, kept
above the keyboard and the system bars. It stays 3 seconds (or the
caller's time) and 70 ms a character more, up to 8, is read out to a
screen reader, and a new toast takes the place of the one before.
BotToast stays as it is (1.9).

U68: logging out other devices (a row, all others, the new device's
[아님]) adds, by the server's mode, that on a staff-only server those
devices cannot connect without the access password until they log in
again, and that HJViewer run without installing it stops accepting
connections too. A login that hjv-api ends with a 401 (not this
device's own logout) shows once "이 기기의 로그인이 끝났습니다" with why
and, by the mode, what it takes now, with [닫기] [로그인]. G2 does not
show on a PC whose binding remains. Rust's ticket request still only
counts a 401 (needs a bridge change).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
